. 
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. * Speed. The simulations run in a compiled plugin on several threads.
. * cores(1) uses one thread, the default uses all physical cores. The
. * results for a given seed are identical.
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. display e(engine)
native

. timer clear

. timer on 1

. quietly nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity gwesp(.69) indegpopularity
>  outactivity seed(4) cores(1)

. timer off 1

. matrix b1 = e(b)

. timer on 2

. quietly nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity gwesp(.69) indegpopularity
>  outactivity seed(4)

. timer off 2

. matrix b2 = e(b)

. display "largest difference between the two sets of estimates: " mreldif(b1, b2)
largest difference between the two sets of estimates: 0

. timer list
   1:      1.33 /        1 =       1.3290
   2:      0.68 /        1 =       0.6830

. 
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. * The length of the estimation: k0() simulations in phase 1, k3()
. * in phase 3. More simulations give smaller convergence t-ratios
. * and a steadier covariance matrix.
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2 glasgow3) outdegree reciprocity gwesp(.69) seed(4) k0(100) k3(3000
> ) detail
